# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# setup: iderunboardinput
# board: discover
# A program on a board asks, and is answered from the message window.
#
# INPUT on a board waits for a person who is at this machine.  The
# window that shows what the program prints is where it asks, and the
# answer typed there reaches the program: proven by a line that goes
# wrong only for that answer, whose error the row then offers to visit.
wait 60
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Programming
wait 4
menu-pick TikuBasic
wait 150
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title Open
click 400 220
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title Open
click-window Project
wait 8
note the row the list stands on is the asking one
key Down
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Run on tiku
note the program asks before it prints anything: the window is made for
note the question, and the question is what the strip shows
wait 200
expect-title Messages
click-window Messages
wait 8
key t
key i
key k
key u
wait 4
key Return
wait 200
note answered with the one word line 20 trips on: its error is the first
note row, and the row knows the line
click-window Messages
wait 8
key Down
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Go to line 20
quit
